The board file makes the SoC's USB controller a gadget as well as a host, which the kernel's
host-only driver reports as a configuration mismatch at every boot, and has the SD driver read a
write-protect switch that microSD slots lack. A later definition of a node overrides an earlier one.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2835-rpi-zero.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2835-rpi-zero.dts
@@ -117,3 +117,12 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart0_gpio14>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+// lfs: overrides of the board file
+&usb {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+};
+
+&sdhost {
+	disable-wp;
+};
